  "message": "I checked with toyota_mechanic: DIAGNOSIS only — nothing was changed.\n\nThe bug: in `voice_io.py`, `_split_sentences` skips the artificial sentence-pause only for abbreviations listed in `_ABBREVIATIONS`. `\"etc\"` isn't in that set, so `\"...income, etc. We will sort...\"` gets split into two sentences, inserting a spurious 0.35s pause (and an extra TTS call) right after \"etc.\" — the same class of bug as the earlier \"Dr.\" / \"9 a.m.\" fixes.\n\nSuggested name: **\"orphaned mid-sentence abbreviation split\"** (this specific case: the **\"etc.\" pause-before-period gap**).\n\nFix would be one line — add `\"etc\"` to `_ABBREVIATIONS` — but no code was touched in this diagnose-only run.",
